      "message": "Let\u0027s assume that `baz` is also in the same APEX. Then `foo` can\u0027t use private APIs from `baz` unless it explicitly uses `libs: [\"baz.impl\"]`, which I want to avoid.   Alternatively, `foo` could drop `sdk_version`(as is done in the second test), but that has its own downside; it will prevent `foo` from depending on any java_sdk_library that is outside of the APEX.\n\nSo, I think this should best be handled automatically by the build system.\n\n`libs: [\"baz\"]` shall be redirected to `baz.stub` or `baz.impl` depending on whether `foo` and `bar` are in the same APEX or not. apex_availability check can be implemented by letting them to report differently on `DepIsInSameApex`; only `baz.impl` should return true.\n\nsdk_version of foo will be ignored for the dependency to baz.impl. It will however be used to select stubs from outside of the APEX, as is currently implemented.",
